I’m afraid I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services such as the Google Geocoding API from here. However, the pair you supplied—**latitude = 37.4224764, longitude = ‑122.0842499**—is already a valid geographic coordinate. It points to the Googleplex (Google’s headquarters) in Mountain View, California.

If you were to feed those numbers into the Geocoding API yourself, you would receive a response similar to:

```json
{
  "results": [
    {
      "address_components": [...],
      "formatted_address": "1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA",
      ...
    }
  ],
  "status": "OK"
}
```

So the coordinates you provided are correct; they simply map to that address.
